{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_z4bfg4wqvis6zyxfzhkf3e5jouc3xc4vgo37jc3qbzle45amp77q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01AJ1XJcEk1iUABZGL57unEs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oSbXCS/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table (Phase C)\n\nMechanically derived from `c_src/src/main.c`. The file contains **no** `assert`,\n**no** `NULL` check, **no** error enum and **no** `errno` inspection; every\nrejection path is one of the two `printf` + `return 1` blocks, plus the\nsaturation limits inside the `strtol` call it makes.\n\nGrep evidence (whole error surface of the program):\n\n```\n40:  if (argc != 2) {\n41:    printf(\"Error: should only be a single (integer) argument!\\n\");\n42:    return 1;\n47:  if (end == argv[1]) {\n49:    printf(\"Error: first argument must be an integer!\\n\");\n50:    return 1;\n```\n\n`E1` = `Error: should only be a single (integer) argument!\\n` (stdout) + exit 1\n`E2` = `Error: first argument must be an integer!\\n` (stdout) + exit 1\n\n| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✔ |\n|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|---|\n| 1  | `main` | `argc != 2`, `argc == 1` (no operand at all) | `E1` | `err_argc_1_cli`, `err_argc_ffi` | [x] |\n| 2  | `main` | `argc != 2`, `argc == 0` (empty argv, reachable via FFI/`execve`) | `E1` | `err_argc_ffi` | [x] |\n| 3  | `main` | `argc != 2`, `argc == 3` (one operand too many) | `E1` | `err_argc_3_cli`, `err_argc_ffi` | [x] |\n| 4  | `main` | `argc != 2`, `argc` large (4 … 64 operands) | `E1` | `err_argc_many_cli`, `err_argc_ffi` | [x] |\n| 5  | `main` | `argc != 2`, `argc` negative (`-1`, `INT_MIN`) — C compares the raw `int`, so a bogus value crossing the FFI boundary must take the same branch | `E1` | `err_argc_negative_ffi` | [x] |\n| 6  | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: `argv[1]` is the empty string `\"\"` | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 7  | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: `argv[1]` is whitespace only (`\" \"`, `\"\\t\"`, `\"\\n\"`, `\"\\v\"`, `\"\\f\"`, `\"\\r\"`, mixes) — `strtol` skips the space, then finds no digit | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 8  | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: sign only (`\"+\"`, `\"-\"`, `\"--\"`, `\"+-\"`, `\"-+3\"`) | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 9  | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: first non-space character is neither sign nor digit (`\"abc\"`, `\"x1\"`, `\".5\"`, `\"/9\"`, `\":0\"`, `\"e5\"`, `\"#\"`) — note `'/'` = `'0'-1` and `':'` = `'9'+1`, the exact digit-range boundaries | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*`, `err_digit_boundary_chars` | [x] |\n| 10 | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: sign immediately followed by a non-digit (`\"+a\"`, `\"-x\"`, `\"+ 1\"`, `\"- 1\"`, `\"+.1\"`) | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 11 | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: whitespace, then sign, then non-digit (`\" +z\"`, `\"\\t-\"`), and space *inside* the number (`\" + 1\"`) | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 12 | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: base-10 `strtol` rejects hex/binary prefixes without digits (`\"0x\"` parses `0` → accepted, but `\"x10\"`, `\"#10\"`, `\"b1\"` are rejected) | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 13 | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: non-ASCII / high-bit bytes (`\"\\xff\"`, `\"é\"`, `\"\\x80\\x81\"`) — not `isspace`/digit in the \"C\" locale | `E2` | `err_non_utf8_arg` | [x] |\n| 14 | `main` | `end == argv[1]`: locale-specific separators that are *not* accepted (`\",\"`, `\"_\"`, `\"'\"`) | `E2` | `err_no_conversion_*` | [x] |\n| 15 | `main` | embedded NUL: `\"\\0\" `/ `\"1\\0 2\"` — C sees a shorter C string; `\"\\0…\"` ⇒ `E2`, `\"1\\0…\"` ⇒ accepted as `1` | `E2` / accept | `err_embedded_nul` | [x] |\n| 16 | `main` | *no* rejection although out of range: `strtol` range error (`ERANGE`) saturates to `LONG_MAX` / `LONG_MIN` and the program ignores it, then truncates to `int` (`\"9223372036854775808\"` → `-1`, `\"-9223372036854775809\"` → `0`) | accepted, exit 0 | `err_range_saturation`, `cfg` rows 18–21 | [x] |\n| 17 | `main` | *no* rejection for values outside `int` range (`\"4294967296\"` → `0`, `\"2147483648\"` → `-2147483648`) — silent truncation, not an error | accepted, exit 0 | `cfg` rows 16–17 | [x] |\n| 18 | `main` | *no* rejection for trailing garbage (`\"5abc\"`, `\"3 4\"`, `\"7\\n\"`) — `end != argv[1]`, so the prefix is used | accepted, exit 0 | `cfg` row 12 | [x] |\n| 19 | `static_sum` | has **no** error path (no checks, no sentinel); `int` overflow of `sum += update` is UB in C but wraps on the target ABI. Verified to wrap identically instead of trapping. | wrapping `int` result | `ffi_static_sum_overflow` | [x] |\n| 20 | `main` (write path) | output cannot be written: stdout redirected to a closed pipe ⇒ `SIGPIPE` (status 141 / signal 13); stdout `/dev/full` ⇒ `ENOSPC` ignored, exit 0 | signal 13 / exit 0 | `err_epipe_kills_process`, `err_dev_full_ignored` | [x] |\n| 21 | `main` | `argc == 2` but `argv[1] == NULL` | UB in C (`strtol(NULL)` → SIGSEGV). Both builds fault; deliberately **not** asserted, documented only. | — (documented) | [x] |\n\nNon-triggers deliberately double-checked (they look like errors but are not):\n`\"0\"`, `\"+0\"`, `\"-0\"`, `\"0000\"`, `\"0x10\"` (→ `0`), `\" 7\"`, very long digit runs\n(200 digits), and `\"2147483647\"`.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":51503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":618,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bf0fff8-6e9f-4845-be1f-6a8b3c8a7388","uuid":"c874c666-0912-4775-ba35-7aa8ec2d30e7","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:29:21.157Z"}
